# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — the academic graph is built from both of these and
# will not start without them. Do not restore the rules below.
#
#   services/data-engineering/data/raw/**/*.json     semester course offerings
#   services/data-engineering/data/catalog_valut/    wiki vault (already tracked)
#
# The graph needs BOTH halves. The vault is committed (2,780 files); the seven
# semester JSON files are what a clone is missing, and without them the engine
# builds with 2,753 wiki pages, 0 courses and 0 prerequisite edges. That is not
# a loud failure: `build_wiring` then registers none of `prerequisite_edges`,
# `track_courses`, `passed_courses` or `remaining_courses`, and the advisor
# quietly loses every curriculum answer while still replying about credits.
# Restoring these rules re-creates that, and the reason is not visible from the
# symptom -- it cost a full session to trace once already.
#
# `scripts/bootstrap-semester-data.sh` is NOT a substitute: its fixtures hold six
# courses between three files, and `wiring._graph_has_usable_catalog` rejects a
# catalog that small on purpose, because answering from it is worse than
# declining.
#
# These files are Technion source data. If a licensing decision means they
# cannot be committed, the fix is to publish the retrieval path they feed --
# not to ignore them silently and let the capability disappear.

# # Generated data-engineering artifacts (local extraction outputs)
# services/data-engineering/data/generated/**
# !services/data-engineering/data/generated/**/README.md

# Large generated quality reports (commit markdown summary or sample JSON only)
services/data-engineering/data/reports/technion/dds_staging_quality_report.json

